# How to cite this project. GitHub shows it as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads it when it archives a release
# (paper/submission.yaml, roadmap M50.1). Keep `version` equal to opengonio.__version__ (tools/paper_check.py checks).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this hardware, software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Open Source Gonioreflectometer (OpenGonio): a printable four-axis BRDF instrument and 3D scanner"
abstract: >-
  A gonioreflectometer and turntable 3D scanner built from 3D-printed parts, stepper motors and a USB camera, without
  soldering, with the opengonio Python package for control, calibration, BRDF fitting, scanning and glTF rendering.
authors:
  - family-names: Norman
    given-names: Aleksander
    affiliation: "California State University, Dominguez Hills"
version: "0.7.0"
license:
  - CERN-OHL-S-2.0
  - GPL-3.0-or-later
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Normansrule/gonioreflectometer-open-source"
url: "https://normansrule.github.io/gonioreflectometer-open-source/"
keywords:
  - BRDF
  - gonioreflectometer
  - material appearance
  - open hardware
  - 3D printing
  - photometric calibration
  - 3D scanning
  - glTF
